From 96dadd91af7f0f0971056ce152adbfadad493ab8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:38:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 36/36] fix(harbor_agent): Terminus-2 resamples after a
 truncated reply, keeping the observation

On a reply that hits max_tokens with nothing salvageable, Harbor 0.25's
Terminus2._query_llm appends the prompt and the truncated reply to the
chat and asks again with "ERROR!! NONE of the actions you just requested
were performed ...". NemoGymLLM attaches the token ids of the last
answered call to the newest assistant message, now the truncated one, and
the token-in endpoint takes them as the exact prefix and adds only the
messages after it. The model so got its previous prompt + reply + the
ERROR and never the prompt, i.e. the output of the commands that did run:
619 turns in 412 of 1302 trials of job 5356101.

Terminus2NemoGym's _query_llm override (the 0035 counter) now takes the
two messages back off in the nested call, which only Terminus2's re-ask
makes, and asks again with the original prompt: a fresh sample of the
same request. The ids stay on the reply they were generated for, the
chat and rollout_details hold answered calls only (Chat and NemoGymLLM
record a call only after the finish_reason check), and
max_consecutive_truncations still ends the episode. Harbor's salvage path
is unchanged.

truncation_retry: harbor (default resample) keeps Terminus2's re-ask; the
kwarg joins SHARED_AGENT_KWARGS, so OpenCode and mini drop it.

Signed-off-by: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
